{"continue":{"clcontinue":"91910373|Documents_from_the_National_Transportation_Library_(US)","continue":"||imageinfo"},"query":{"pages":{"81848649":{"pageid":81848649,"ns":6,"title":"File:1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe (32508937087).jpg","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4422920,"width":5184,"height":3456,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg/960px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":640,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg/1920px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg/960px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":640,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg/1920px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508937087%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_(32508937087).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=81848649","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2019-09-03 17:45:15","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe (32508937087)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Australia photographs taken on 2019-03-23|1968 Mercury Cougar|Photographs by Sicnag","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"-38.039844","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"145.364398","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Edsel Ford introduced the Mercury in 1939 as a marque to fill the gap between the basic Ford, and the luxury Lincoln.\nThe Mercury Cougar was based on Fords pony car, the Mustang from 1967-73, then the Ford Torino form 1974-80.\nThe first generation Cougar was built from 1967-70, it was 3 inches longer than the Mustang and more luxurious. \nIn 1967, it got a full-width divided 'electric shaver' grille with hidden headlamps. Only available as a two door Hardtop, it was available in base or the luxury XR-7 (woodgrain dash and steering wheel, centre and overhead consoles). Base engine was the 200hp 289 V8. The GT Performance package was available on both models (390 V8, upgraded suspension and better brakes)\nIn 1968, the Cougar got side marker lights, the 210hp 302 was now the base engine on XR-7s (289 still in the base model), the 335hp 428 was available on the GT. \n619 XR-7Gs were produced, any engine but they got hood scoop, fog lamps, and hood pins.\nThe new GT-E package; 357 built with the 390hp 427 V8 and 37 built with the 410hp 428SCJ.   \n</p>\n1969 saw a facelift, new model names and a convertible was available.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2019-03-23 09:37","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/42220226@N07/32508937087/\">1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/42220226@N07\">Sicnag</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-2.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}],"categories":[{"ns":14,"title":"Category:1968 Mercury Cougar"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Australia photographs taken on 2019-03-23"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:CC-BY-2.0"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Photographs by Sicnag"}]},"81848648":{"pageid":81848648,"ns":6,"title":"File:1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe (32508939497).jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4706070,"width":5184,"height":3456,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg/960px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":640,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg/1920px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg/960px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":640,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg/1920px-1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_%2832508939497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1968_Mercury_Cougar_XR-7_Coupe_(32508939497).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=81848648","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2019-09-03 17:45:15","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe (32508939497)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Australia photographs taken on 2019-03-23|1968 Mercury Cougar|Photographs by Sicnag","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"-38.039844","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"145.364398","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Edsel Ford introduced the Mercury in 1939 as a model to fill the gap between the basic Ford, and the luxury Lincoln.\nThe Mercury Cougar was based on Fords pony car, the Mustang from 1967-73, then the Ford Torino form 1974-80.\nThe first generation Cougar was built from 1967-70, it was 3 inches longer than the Mustang and more luxurious. \nIn 1967, it got a full-width divided 'electric shaver' grille with hidden headlamps. Only available as a two door Hardtop, it was available in base or the luxury XR-7 (woodgrain dash and steering wheel, centre and overhead consoles). Base engine was the 200hp 289 V8. The GT Performance package was available on both models (390 V8, upgraded suspension and better brakes)\nIn 1968, the Cougar got side marker lights, the 210hp 302 was now the base engine on XR-7s (289 still in the base model), the 335hp 428 was available on the GT. \n619 XR-7Gs were produced, any engine but they got hood scoop, fog lamps, and hood pins.\nThe new GT-E package; 357 built with the 390hp 427 V8 and 37 built with the 410hp 428SCJ.   \n</p>\n1969 saw a facelift, new model names and a convertible was available.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2019-03-23 09:38","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/42220226@N07/32508939497/\">1968 Mercury Cougar XR-7 Coupe</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/42220226@N07\">Sicnag</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-2.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}],"categories":[{"ns":14,"title":"Category:1968 Mercury Cougar"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Australia photographs taken on 2019-03-23"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:CC-BY-2.0"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Photographs by Sicnag"}]},"64094575":{"pageid":64094575,"ns":6,"title":"File:1978 Ford Mustang II King Cobra Hatchback (30237716893).jpg","index":4,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":5403250,"width":5184,"height":3456,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg/960px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":640,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg/1920px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg/960px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":640,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg/1920px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_(30237716893).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=64094575","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2017-11-15 22:54:57","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"1978 Ford Mustang II King Cobra Hatchback (30237716893)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Images with extracted images|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation|Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2|Australia photographs taken on 2016-10-30|Photographs by Sicnag|Ford Mustang II King Cobra","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"-38.039844","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"145.364398","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Bright Red. \nFords Pony car, the Mustang was first introduced in April, 1964.\nWith the 1974-78 second generation, Lee Iacocca wanted to bring the Mustang back to a small, sporty, luxurious, personal car to follow the world trend. The Mustang II, the first Mustang to be offered with a 4 cyl. (used until 1993)\nSimulating the earlier Shelbys, the Cobra II appearance package was introduced in 1976 with simulated hood scoop, front and rear spoilers and cobra-themed graphics. Note, hood scoops went from facing forward in 76 to facing rearward in 77. The King Cobra, (4313 made) got a cobra snake decal on the hood was available in 1978.\nThe T top was an option in 1977 on only the Hatchback\nTwo body styles were available, the 2 door Hardtop Coupe with woodgrain instrument panel and the 3 door Hatchback with brushed aluminium instrument panel. \nThe Coupe available in Standard or the luxury Ghia, the Ghia, from 1975, with opera windows and vinyl roof.\nThe Hatchback available in Standard or the V6 Mach 1. The sporty Mach got dual tail pipes, and a Tu-Tone paint job, black on the lower body and rear taillight panel.\n</p>\nEngines; 88hp 140 cu in 4 cyl, 105hp 171 cu in V6 and 134hp 302 V8","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-10-30 10:07","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/42220226@N07/30237716893/\">1978 Ford Mustang II King Cobra Hatchback</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/42220226@N07\">Sicnag</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution 2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Copyrighted":{"value":"True","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"cc-by-2.0","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}],"categories":[{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Australia photographs taken on 2016-10-30"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:CC-BY-2.0"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Flickr images reviewed by FlickreviewR 2"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Ford Mustang II King Cobra"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Images with extracted images"},{"ns":14,"title":"Category:Photographs by Sicnag"}]},"143388403":{"pageid":143388403,"ns":6,"title":"File:1978 Ford Mustang II King Cobra Hatchback (30237716893) (cropped).jpg","index":3,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3550521,"width":4257,"height":2840,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":960,"thumbheight":640,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1920px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":960,"height":640,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1920px-1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/12/1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_%2830237716893%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1978_Ford_Mustang_II_King_Cobra_Hatchback_(30237716893)_(cropped).jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=143388403","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2024-01-01 23:36:07","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"1978 Ford Mustang II King Cobra Hatchback (30237716893) (cropped)","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Extracted images|Files with coordinates missing SDC location of creation|Australia photographs taken on 2016-10-30|Photographs by Sicnag|Ford Mustang II King Cobra","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"GPSLatitude":{"value":"-38.039844","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSLongitude":{"value":"145.364398","source":"commons-desc-page"},"GPSMapDatum":{"value":"WGS-84","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Bright Red. \nFords Pony car, the Mustang was first introduced in April, 1964.\nWith the 1974-78 second generation, Lee Iacocca wanted to bring the Mustang back to a small, sporty, luxurious, personal car to follow the world trend. The Mustang II, the first Mustang to be offered with a 4 cyl. (used until 1993)\nSimulating the earlier Shelbys, the Cobra II appearance package was introduced in 1976 with simulated hood scoop, front and rear spoilers and cobra-themed graphics. Note, hood scoops went from facing forward in 76 to facing rearward in 77. The King Cobra, (4313 made) got a cobra snake decal on the hood was available in 1978.\nThe T top was an option in 1977 on only the Hatchback\nTwo body styles were available, the 2 door Hardtop Coupe with woodgrain instrument panel and the 3 door Hatchback with brushed aluminium instrument panel. \nThe Coupe available in Standard or the luxury Ghia, the Ghia, from 1975, with opera windows and vinyl roof.\nThe Hatchback available in Standard or the V6 Mach 1. The sporty Mach got dual tail pipes, and a Tu-Tone paint job, black on the lower body and rear taillight panel.\n</p>\nEngines; 88hp 140 cu in 4 cyl, 105hp 171 cu in V6 and 134hp 302 V8","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-10-30 10:07","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=